-- title:
--   Distinct ends are not contained in the Igusa branch Wₓ
-- statement:
--   The data fall into several blocks.
--
--   Base arithmetic data. A prime $q\ge 5$; a natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero; an element $\xi\in L$ that is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι`, that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Next, an intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ with `hK` asserting that $K$ is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $((q\ell)^2M',\ \mathtt{levelH}(q\ell)M')$, i.e. the field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images, under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the rational $q$-expansions of the modular functions of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   The base ring. A discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain, an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction field, Henselian local with algebraically closed residue field; $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAq`), and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. An element $j\in K$, nonzero, whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$ pushed from $\mathbb Q$ to $L$. A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ (`hϖ`), and an element $\varpi_t$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   The supersingular point. A maximal ideal $y$ of the chart algebra $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ — the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ — containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), together with `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The Drinfeld-chart package `hArig` (seven clauses, summarised here). For every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $\mathtt{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ pulled back from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\mathtt{XFin}=\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin})$ above $z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv \mathtt{drinfeldForm}\,q\,W=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu)$, subject to seven conditions: $e$ carries constants from $A$ to $C\circ\sigma$; the automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ that are level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ (the predicate `IsLevelAutAt`, which says that after transport to $\mathbb C$-coefficients along an embedding sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, $\tau$ acts on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ by the slash action of $\mathtt{conjElemN}(q\ell)\gamma^{-1}$) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve the chart algebra; for $\gamma$ also in $\Gamma(\ell)$ the induced endomorphism is the identity modulo $y'$; such $\tau$ trivial modulo $y'$ are realised on $S$ by an automorphism $\theta$ fixing constants, acting on $X_0,X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ by a matrix $M$ congruent to $c\gamma$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$ with $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, with $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $c\not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; primes of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ with distinct tangent directions $(a_1:b_1)$, $(a_2:b_2)$ modulo $q$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime with tangent direction $(1:0)$, membership of $\mathtt{germ}(a)$ in its contraction is equivalent to all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lying in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$; and the element $\mathtt{jqNModC}\,L\,(q\ell)$ lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and, after subtracting a suitable $a_0\in A$ congruent to it modulo $y'$, corresponds to a series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge 1$ whose $e_0$-th homogeneous form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b)\in W^2$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q$ in the maximal ideal.
--
--   A fixed point and chart. The point $z$, germ $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz`, `hz` as above; a point $y'$ of $\mathtt{XFin}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y')=z$ (`hy'`), satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$ (`hy'y`). Further, an explicit instance of the package: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with `hσ₁`, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completed stalk at $z$ onto $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$, and the hypothesis `hW₁` asserting for this data exactly the seven clauses listed above.
--
--   The blow-up ideal and chart. An ideal $J$ of the chart algebra with `hJ`: $J$ is the infimum of the ideals obtained, as $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart algebra, as the pullback along $\tau$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathtt{toC}\circ\mathtt{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. A subalgebra $B$ of $K$ over $A$ with `hB`: $B$ is the chart-algebra subalgebra generated by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ x\,\varpi_t=i\}$, viewed over $A$ — the blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   The valuation subring $W$ and its properties. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`); `hR1`: the chart algebra is contained in $B$, and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; `hR2`: $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses): $W$ meets $L$ exactly in $A$, the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, the centre of $W$ cuts out $y$ on the chart algebra, and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at that centre. `hEQ` (five clauses): for each $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathtt{CoordRing}\,q\,(\text{residue field})$ whose kernel is the centre of $W$, compatible with $A\to$ residue field, and equivariant for the level automorphisms preserving $W$ through an element $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of $\mathtt{hSubgroup}\,q$ acting by $\mathtt{hAction}$, with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; level automorphisms preserve $B$; every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained from the centre of $W$ by some such $\tau$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; an element of $B$ carried into the centre by all such $\tau$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and a level automorphism preserving $y$ on the chart algebra preserves $W$.
--
--   The Igusa-invariant element and the exponent. Hypotheses `hjK`, `hjC`: $\mathtt{jqNModC}\,L\,(q\ell)$, the $q$-expansion of $j$ with $q$ replaced by $q^{q\ell}$, lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra. A natural number $m\ge1$ with $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hmt`).
--
--   The ends. A finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K$, characterised by `hends`: a subring $O$ lies in $\mathrm{ends}$ precisely when there are $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$, and, writing $B_a$ for the chart-algebra subalgebra generated over $A$ by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ xa=i\}$, a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (membership in $O$ means being a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$), every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B$ is not contained in $O$.
--
--   The distinguished end $O$ and its crossing data. An element $O\in\mathrm{ends}$ (`hOmem`) with: $O\subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), the chart algebra contained in $O$ (`hCO`), $\varpi\in O$ (`hϖO`); elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, and an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}$ of the $\varpi$-adic completion $\hat A$ of $A$ at $\varpi^m$, i.e. $\hat A[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\varpi^m)$, together with units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that ring and the conditions $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ (`hcxy`), $\iota$ sends elements of $A$ to constants (`hιc`), $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ (`hιx`), $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$ (`hιy`), $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$ (`hcyW`) and $c_x$ does not (`hcxW`).
--
--   The Igusa branch. A valuation subring $W_x$ of $K$ with: $O\subseteq W_x$ (`hB0`); the chart algebra contained in $W_x$ (`hB1`); $W_x$ meets $L$ exactly in $A$ (`hB2`); $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring (`hB3`); the maximal ideal of $W_x$ generated by $\varpi$ (`hB4`); `hB6`, residual transcendence of $\mathtt{jqNModC}\,L\,(q\ell)$: for every polynomial $p$ over $A$, if the value at that element of the polynomial with coefficients pushed to $L$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, then all coefficients of $p$ lie in the maximal ideal of $A$; $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ (`hB7`) and $c_y$ outside it (`hB8`); every element of the chart algebra lying in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ lies in $y$ (`hB9`); and some element of $y$ lies outside the maximal ideal of $W_x$ (`hB10`).
--
--   Conclusion. For every $O'\in\mathrm{ends}$ with $O'\ne O$ there exists $f\in K$ with $f\in O'$ and $f\notin W_x$; that is, no end other than $O$ is contained in $W_x$.
--
--   This is the geometric step separating the ends of the exceptional fibre of the blow-up at a supersingular point: the Igusa branch through the distinguished end $O$, realised as the valuation subring $W_x$, contains no other end of the blow-up charts $C[J/a]$. It feeds the construction of the Igusa valuation subring attached to an end in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaValuationSubring_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaValuationSubring_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), and rests on [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_not_mem_iff_mem_of_ne_of_mem_ends_igusaBranch_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_not_mem_iff_mem_of_ne_of_mem_ends_igusaBranch_linked).
